To run Katana, use the basic terminal command structure followed by flags to control the crawl depth and output targets.
## Basic Crawl
To scan a single website and discover its basic links, endpoints, and assets:

katana -u https://example.com

## Crawl Multiple Targets
To scan multiple websites at the same time, save your URLs into a text file (e.g., targets.txt) and pass it to the tool:

katana -list targets.txt

## Advanced Scanning Configurations
Combine flags to maximize discovery:

* Deep Scan with JS Parsing (Finds endpoints hidden inside JavaScript files):

katana -u https://example.com -jc -d 3

* Headless Mode (Uses a real background browser to find links rendered by heavy single-page apps like React or Angular):

katana -u https://example.com -headless

* Save Output to a File (Saves all discovered endpoints to a clean text file):

katana -u https://example.com -o results.txt


------------------------------
## Commonly Used Flags

* -u : The target URL to scan.
* -jc : Parses and extracts endpoints from JavaScript files (similar to LinkFinder).
* -d : Set crawl depth limit (default is 3).
* -headless : Enables headless browser crawling.
* -o : File path to write output results.

